FileUploadApi/
│
├── Controllers/
│   └── FileController.cs
│       - Handles all HTTP endpoints:
│           • Upload single file by type
│           • Upload multiple files by type
│           • Get files (all or by type)
│
├── Services/
│   ├── IFileService.cs
│       - Interface for file service
│           • SaveFileAsync
│           • SaveMultipleFilesAsync
│           • GetUploadedFiles
│
│   ├── FileService.cs
│       - Main implementation
│           • Saves files to folders
│           • Updates files.json with metadata
│           • Performs type-specific validation
│
│   ├── BestPracticeService.cs  (optional)
│       - Handles PDF-specific rules
│
│   ├── LessonsLearnedService.cs (optional)
│       - Handles image-specific rules
│
│   └── MeetingNotesService.cs (optional)
│       - Handles text file-specific rules
│
├── Models/
│   ├── FileMetadataDto.cs
│       - Represents a file: Name, Path, UploadDate, Type
│
│   ├── ApiResponse.cs
│       - Standard API response wrapper: Success, Message, Data
│
│   └── ErrorResponse.cs
│       - Structure for error details
│
├── Constants/
│   └── RouteValue.cs
│       - Holds route strings for endpoints
│
├── UploadedFiles/
│   ├── BestPractice/         - Stores PDF files
│   ├── LessonsLearned/       - Stores images (jpg/png)
│   └── MeetingNotes/         - Stores text files
│
├── files.json
│   - Stores metadata for all uploaded files
│     Fields: FileName, FilePath, UploadDate, FileType
│
├── Program.cs
│   - Sets up ASP.NET Core app
│
└── Startup.cs
    - Configures services, dependency injectionHow to Test the Output
Upload a file
Endpoint: POST /api/file/upload/{fileType}
Test with:
PDF for BestPractice
JPG/PNG for LessonsLearned
TXT for MeetingNotes
Expected output:
File saved in UploadedFiles/{fileType}
Metadata added in files.json
Response returns success and file info
Upload multiple files
Endpoint: POST /api/file/upload-multiple/{fileType}
Same rules as above
Get all files
Endpoint: GET /api/file/files
Expected output:
JSON array of all files with metadata
Get files by type
Endpoint: GET /api/file/files?fileType=BestPractice (or LessonsLearned / MeetingNotes)
Expected output:
JSON array filtered by the requested type
Error handling
Upload wrong file type → API returns failure with error message
Upload empty file → API returns failure
Try GET when files.json doesn’t exist → API returns empty array
